<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#special-administrative-regions-of-china">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Special administrative regions of China</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Special Administrative Region</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The special administrative regions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> are <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macau">Macau</a>, created under the principle of 'one country, two systems' when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> returned Hong Kong in 1997 and Portugal returned Macau in 1999. Each has its own Basic Law, legal system, currency and customs territory, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> controls defence and foreign affairs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/special-administrative-regions-of-china.jpg" alt="Special administrative regions of China" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alanmak, Serg!o, ASDFGH · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:China-Special_Administrative_Regions.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
